  "reason": "The first full 129-case product-gate run (#129) found two defects in the frozen react-output-v1 test tools. First, in reference/src/app.test.tsx, the list test \"lists rows with the first page query\" counted screen.getAllByText(String(sample(first))) across the whole page and expected 2; when another column rendered the same text (such as multiple bool fields rendering true), the count was 3 to 7 instead of 2 (60 legacy100 products). The test now checks that the table has 2 data rows (tbody tr) and that in each data row the FIELDS[0] cell (column index 1, right after id) has text String(sample(FIELDS[0])). Second, in tests/react-output-v1/api_contract.mjs, sample(field, \"changed\") returned the same value as the full row for int (7), float (1.5) and date (2026-01-05), causing a 409 conflict when patching a unique non-str first field (legacy100-0012 and legacy100-0030). sample(field, \"changed\") now returns 19 for int, 4.5 for float and \"2026-04-01\" for date, and api-contract.json samples records those values.",
